    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/maps_cli.py, release no longer writes the local bundle.json before the push: stage_bundle already carries the version into the staged copy, so the local version is written only after push_tree returns, and the read-and-restore of the original bytes on push failure is removed because nothing local changes before the push. _write_bundle_version writes atomically, to a temporary file in the same directory followed by os.replace, so neither a reader nor an interrupted write ever sees a partial descriptor. tests/test_maps_cli.py gains a test whose stubbed push_tree reads the local bundle.json while it runs and asserts it still names the previous version, and a test that makes the atomic replace raise and asserts the original bundle.json bytes are intact. The existing failed-push test still passes. All tests use the stubbed registry with no network call. tests/test_maps_cli.py runs whole at base and head, each captured to a log ending in the pytest summary and an EXIT line, and adds no failure. uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests packages exits 0.",
